---
// The colophon (section 4.1): how the site is built, the fonts, the stack, the
// design idea, the testing, and the AI disclosure in one paragraph (7.2).
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { STATIC_PAGES } from "../lib/pages";
import { webPage } from "../lib/seo/jsonld";
import { canonicalUrl } from "../lib/seo/meta";

const page = STATIC_PAGES.colophon;
---

<Base
  title={page.title}
  description={page.description}
  path={page.path}
  jsonLd={[
    webPage({ url: canonicalUrl(page.path), title: page.title, description: page.description }),
  ]}
>
  <article class="wrap colophon">
    <header class="colophon__header">
      <p class="eyebrow">{page.eyebrow}</p>
      <h1>How this site is built</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="colophon__sections">
      <section aria-labelledby="words">
        <h2 id="words">The words</h2>
        <p>
          [MICHAEL: confirm or rewrite this paragraph; it is the AI disclosure from the plan. Draft:
          Every word on this site was written or edited by me. I use Claude Code to build and to
          draft from my own interview transcripts, and I edit every draft by ear with a screen
          reader before it goes up. The memoir chapters are mine alone. A pattern check runs over
          every string on the site, down to the button labels, and rejects the tells of machine
          writing, so what you read here sounds like me because it is.]
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="idea">
        <h2 id="idea">The idea</h2>
        <p>
          The home page moves from darkness to light as you scroll: it opens on near-black and the
          ground steps up to paper by the time you reach the writing. It is the arc of the memoir
          turned into a layout. Every text color is checked against every ground.
        </p>
        <p>The mark in the header is the braille cells for M and W. It is the favicon too.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="type">
        <h2 id="type">Type</h2>
        <p>
          Headings are set in Fraunces. Body text is Atkinson Hyperlegible Next, designed by the
          Braille Institute for low-vision legibility; it tells I, l and 1 apart, and O from 0,
          which helps everyone. Code, dates and small labels are JetBrains Mono. All three are
          self-hosted and subsetted, with fallbacks sized to match so nothing jumps when they load.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="stack">
        <h2 id="stack">Stack</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Astro builds every page to plain HTML at deploy; a post page carries no framework code
            at all.
          </li>
          <li>
            Vercel hosts it and runs the two small functions (the contact form and the metrics job)
            and the nightly cron.
          </li>
          <li>
            Supabase holds the live numbers, a backup of contact messages and the newsletter mirror.
            Every table has row level security.
          </li>
          <li>
            Resend sends the contact mail. Buttondown runs the newsletter. Giscus, built on GitHub
            Discussions, handles comments and loads only when you ask for it.
          </li>
          <li>
            Google Analytics 4 counts visits, loaded after the page is interactive, with no
            advertising features. The <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a> says what it stores.
          </li>
          <li>Pagefind indexes the site at deploy, so search works with no server.</li>
          <li>
            Expressive Code renders code blocks. satori and sharp draw a social image for every page
            at build.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="rules">
        <h2 id="rules">Rules the site follows</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Every image has alt text. Images that carry information also have a long description
            under "Describe this image", for everyone.
          </li>
          <li>Every chart has a data table.</li>
          <li>Every number is real and shows its source and date.</li>
          <li>Nothing moves unless you scroll, and nothing plays unless you press play.</li>
          <li>Focus is always visible. Nothing depends on hover, pointer precision or a mouse.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          The <a href="/accessibility">accessibility statement</a> has the test process and the fix
          log.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="source">
        <h2 id="source">Source</h2>
        <p>[MICHAEL: say whether the repository is public and link it, or remove this section]</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .colophon {
    padding-block: var(--space-7) var(--space-8);
  }
  .colophon__header h1 {
    font-size: var(--step-5);
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }
  .colophon__sections {
    margin-top: var(--space-7);
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-7);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .colophon__sections h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }
  .colophon__sections p + p,
  .colophon__sections ul + p {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
  }
  .colophon__sections ul {
    padding-left: 1.2em;
  }
  .colophon__sections li + li {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }
</style>
